Pathfinder patch for jaq 3.1.1: Keep a comment at the end of the program inside it.

An unclosed delimiter before a comment that runs to the end of the program
(`[1 #`) made the error report panic (exit 101) where jq reports a compile
error (exit 3). Found by fuzzing (TODO T-019). Applies to 3.1.0 too.

Carried in-tree (Steelbore Standard 4.2, 6.4); not sent upstream.

diff --git a/jaq-core/src/load/lex.rs b/jaq-core/src/load/lex.rs
index 9cd94cf..38c0da5 100644
--- a/jaq-core/src/load/lex.rs
+++ b/jaq-core/src/load/lex.rs
@@ -160,7 +160,10 @@ impl<'a> Lexer<&'a str> {
             }
             // ignore all lines that end with an odd number of backslashes
             loop {
-                let (before, after) = self.i.split_once('\n').unwrap_or((self.i, ""));
+                // Pathfinder: the rest is the empty end of the input, not a
+                // `""` from elsewhere, so that spans into it stay inside it.
+                let end = &self.i[self.i.len()..];
+                let (before, after) = self.i.split_once('\n').unwrap_or((self.i, end));
                 let before = before.strip_suffix('\r').unwrap_or(before);
                 self.i = after;
                 // does the line end with an even number of backslashes?
